    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear strategy focused on exploiting favorable matchups for our high-upside bats. **Kyle Tucker** (75.19) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.55) lead the charge as our strongest plays. **Kyle Tucker** draws a soft landing against Matt Wilkinson; despite the lineup status being pending, the matchup leverage provides his elite floor, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a significant SP Skill boost against Corbin Burnes. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (71.50) is locked into a high-efficiency start, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Sandy Alcantara outweighs the slight park disadvantage. We are also monitoring **Gunnar Henderson** (67.74) closely; while the matchup against the high-velocity Jacob Misiorowski is daunting, the park factors and platoon advantage keep him well within the \"Strong\" start range.\n\nThe bench decision process was narrow today, with **Dominic Smith** (47.50) serving as the most difficult exclusion. While his platoon advantage against Hunter Brown provided a decent floor, he ultimately fell short of the threshold compared to the primary lineup. We also opted to sit **Coby Mayo** (44.90) and **Josh Jung** (43.41), both of whom are capable, but they struggle to outpace the core rotation in this specific 5x5 context. Conversely, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.38), whose matchup against Jacob deGrom suppresses his ceiling. We will keep an eye on **Drake Baldwin**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Luis Lara**\u2014all of whom have pending lineups\u2014as these positions carry the highest volatility risk. Ensure all lineups are confirmed before game time, as any shift in batting order for these targets could significantly alter their projected efficiency.",
